{"aligned_passages":[{"anchor":"weighted-tree","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:8c370b67aa0a6f2b705479e8d6814e78733322389d75881ba1c79f94458dfa9b/papers/long.json","paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=7fffb9c3a87dee62cdc5e1be3d2c95da7815e21efefdd9a493e1852eba958118","passage_ref":"sha256:4c6350e9b4de8b6fa8cb1160f0ada57e4a2b797aebd0c518c88b1ace1b27878b/papers/long.md/sha256:8c370b67aa0a6f2b705479e8d6814e78733322389d75881ba1c79f94458dfa9b/papers/long.json/passages/weighted-tree","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=7fffb9c3a87dee62cdc5e1be3d2c95da7815e21efefdd9a493e1852eba958118&paper=long&passage=weighted-tree","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=7fffb9c3a87dee62cdc5e1be3d2c95da7815e21efefdd9a493e1852eba958118&paper=long&passage=weighted-tree","span":{"end_byte":218570,"end_line":4813,"start_byte":208643,"start_line":4597},"stage":"long"}],"lenses":{"consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=7fffb9c3a87dee62cdc5e1be3d2c95da7815e21efefdd9a493e1852eba958118&view=arguments&node=circuit.weighted_finite_horizon&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=7fffb9c3a87dee62cdc5e1be3d2c95da7815e21efefdd9a493e1852eba958118&node=circuit.weighted_finite_horizon&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=7fffb9c3a87dee62cdc5e1be3d2c95da7815e21efefdd9a493e1852eba958118&node=circuit.weighted_finite_horizon&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=7fffb9c3a87dee62cdc5e1be3d2c95da7815e21efefdd9a493e1852eba958118&view=arguments&node=circuit.weighted_finite_horizon&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=7fffb9c3a87dee62cdc5e1be3d2c95da7815e21efefdd9a493e1852eba958118&ref=sha256%3Af22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92%2Fnodes%2Fcircuit.weighted_finite_horizon","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"Conditional ordinary reconstruction for the specified finite recursion, not a new formal theorem. The coefficient expectation uses the vertex law; its normalization uses the cavity law. Fixed-horizon and spatial-Lipschitz hypotheses are essential. The generic temporal-sign counterexample concerns auxiliary Theorem 4.1 as printed, not specialized positive-Parisi Proposition 4.7 or EAMS Theorem 1.7. No horizon-, temperature- or terminal-cutoff-uniform constant is claimed.","citation_ids":["circuit-r2-26-cite-positive-finite-step","eams2023_finite_step"],"evidence_ids":["ordinary_reconstruction_bounds_20261024"],"id":"circuit.weighted_finite_horizon","kind":"claim","label":"Corrected weighted finite-tree estimate with explicit hypotheses","locator":"07-positive-temperature.tex:211–450; EAMS arXiv:2111.06813v2 Proposition 2.1 and Lemmas 3.2–3.4,4.2–4.3; long §11.1","source_id":"circuit-r2-26-source-positive","statement":"In the specified EAMS one-step-lag recursion on a k-regular tree, k>=2, fix delta>0 and finite L>=1 with L*delta<1. Use iid Gaussian labels and the common node/cavity initial state sqrt(delta)*g_i. At the finitely many mesh times, assume |a_k|<=K>=1, spatial Lipschitz constants La,Lb for a_k,b_k uniform in k, identical normalized a_k for node/cavity updates, and E[(A_(i->j)^r)^2]=1. Then |k*E[z_o^L*z_v^L]-2*sqrt(k-1)*delta*sum_(r=1)^(L-1) E[B_o^r]|<=C(K,La,Lb,delta,L), independently of k. The sum is empty when L=1.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/circuit.weighted_finite_horizon","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"citations","from":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/circuit.positive_finite_step","id":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/edges/%5B%22circuit.positive_finite_step%22%2C%22circuit.weighted_finite_horizon%22%2C%22cites%22%5D","kind":"cites","record_ref":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/edges/%5B%22circuit.positive_finite_step%22%2C%22circuit.weighted_finite_horizon%22%2C%22cites%22%5D","semantic_class":"citation_reference","to":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/circuit.weighted_finite_horizon"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/circuit.weighted_finite_horizon","id":"field:214b814586f0e4d9fc9418f1ac21c753fb7f49570973cfdb295d36182ef0e4b9","kind":"citation_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/circuit.weighted_finite_horizon","semantic_class":"provenance_field_reference","source_field":"citation_ids","to":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/citations/circuit-r2-26-cite-positive-finite-step"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/circuit.weighted_finite_horizon","id":"field:298481aebe48c9b45a3650e6dd565c9f69beca7cd325a304c3d857cb1ef67a9f","kind":"source_id","owner_ref":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/circuit.weighted_finite_horizon","semantic_class":"provenance_field_reference","source_field":"source_id","to":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/sources/circuit-r2-26-source-positive"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/edges/%5B%22circuit.positive_finite_step%22%2C%22circuit.weighted_finite_horizon%22%2C%22cites%22%5D","id":"field:5f1bdf2d9226a2fd33d8855a56c8a17e3749453e41ac7d0eee0fbaf264d40411","kind":"to","owner_ref":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/edges/%5B%22circuit.positive_finite_step%22%2C%22circuit.weighted_finite_horizon%22%2C%22cites%22%5D","semantic_class":"edge_endpoint_reference","source_field":"to","to":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/circuit